WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.300
- And we need to mention everybody

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.450
that Troy is the first deaf male actor

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:06.606
to earn an Oscar nomination
(audience cheering) and to win

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.606
an individual SAG Award.

00:00:09.871 --> 00:00:12.400
I mean it's exciting.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.253
So how does that feel?

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.290
- Of course I'm extremely excited

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:20.280
and it's great to finally be recognized.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:24.280
It means that our peers are
accepting our work as artists,

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:25.380
not because we're deaf,

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.960
we're just actors who happen to be deaf.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.920
And we're being recognized for our talent.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.330
And so I'm so glad.

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:33.490
It's been a long and tough journey for me,

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:34.440
and I feel like I've received

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.473
an honorary PhD when
getting these nominations

00:00:37.473 --> 00:00:38.306
(audience clapping)

00:00:38.306 --> 00:00:40.220
and it's like I'm finally
arrived at their level

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:41.320
and I feel so blessed.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.780
You know the decisions

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.680
that I made in my life brought me here

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.340
but Marlee was such an
important role model

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:51.450
and she kept me alive.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.110
She gave Daniel and I hope.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:54.740
- Yeah definitely.
- And so Marley

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:57.160
was a great representative
for the deaf community

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.910
for so many years, and
now we're able to come up.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:02.004
And so I'm so grateful to Marlee
(audience claps) for that.

00:01:02.004 --> 00:01:04.170
- I agree.
- And it's so interesting

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.870
'cause Marlee we've seen in movies,

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:09.050
I've seen movies, TV, I've
seen Marlee in so many things.

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:10.500
And it's like it's one of those things

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.380
where it's like why are we just seeing one

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:13.213
like one person?

00:01:13.213 --> 00:01:14.090
Like she is amazing

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:15.710
but like there has to
be a whole community.

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:17.410
And I feel like Marlee
was it very important

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.690
for you to be a part of
this movie in particular?

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:21.130
Because it not only showcases

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:23.300
like your gifts, your talent as an actor,

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.130
but also to get help
highlight other actors

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:27.600
that just happen to be deaf

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.760
that love what they do
and excel at what they do.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.740
Is this just such an
important project for you?

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:35.280
- Absolutely I mean it's been
35 years being in the industry

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.670
that I've tried to spread
the message to people

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:41.250
that yes I'm here but
I'm not the only one.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:43.720
There are so many other
deaf actors out there,

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:45.663
deaf directors, deaf writers,

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:50.380
and Coda's, people who
can sign and who can act.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:54.580
And it's sometimes you know
it would fall on deaf ears,

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:55.413
that sounds ironic,

00:01:55.413 --> 00:02:00.380
but it takes collaboration,
it takes one to listen,

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:04.000
to spread the message, it
takes work, it takes homework.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.880
But at the end of the day we are here,

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:10.620
we're focused on doing
whatever it is we can do,

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:13.310
we can continue to make noise.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:16.159
But the key is collaboration,
it's collaboration,

00:02:16.159 --> 00:02:17.609
(audience claps) in all ways.

